{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-013", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["record", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Somnigroup raises sales 10.8%, revises FY26 earnings outlook", "content": "Somnigroup revised FY26 adjusted EPS guidance to $2.85-$2.95 after Q3 sales rose 10.8 per cent YoY to record $2.35 billion.\nLeggett & Platt added $372.6 million after the deal, offsetting 5.8 per cent declines at Mattress Firm and Tempur Sealy North America.\nAdjusted net income rose 13.7 per cent; GAAP net income fell 7.8 per cent as acquisition costs and Dreams disruption weighed on margins.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/us-somnigroup-raises-sales-10-8-revises-fy26-earnings-outlook-314905-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-014", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Yarn policy: How can Bangladesh balance competing interests?", "content": "Bangladesh's garment exporters say NBR orders on bonded-warehouse access for imported cotton yarn have disrupted procurement, raised prices and unsettled buyers.\nBGMEA and BKMEA say policy shifts have disrupted plans, squeezed working capital and could hurt export competitiveness.\nFabric and yarn imports rose 12.33 per cent month-on-month in September, while raw-cotton imports fell 13.38 per", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/yarn-policy-how-can-bangladesh-balance-competing-interests--314882-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-015", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["[否定]decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "T&A imports in US drop 4.88% during Jan-Sept 2026", "content": "US textile and apparel imports fell by 4.88 per cent to $76.358 billion in January–September 2026, with apparel down 5.76 per cent and non-apparel down 2.25 per cent.\nVietnam remained the top supplier with an 18.65 per cent share, ahead of China at 15.07 per cent.\nChina and India posted sharp declines across apparel and non-apparel, while Cambodia, Italy, Vietnam and Indonesia gained.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/t-a-imports-in-us-drop-4-88-during-jan-sept-2026-314870-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-016", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Superior Group tightens FY26 outlook as Q3 sales rise 5%", "content": "Superior Group of Companies has tightened its FY26 sales outlook to $578 million-$585 million and adjusted diluted earnings per share outlook to $0.60-$0.66.\nThird-quarter sales rose 5 per cent year on year to $146 million, led by Branded Products and Contact Centers.\nNet income edged down to $2.6 million as the company advances its Healthcare Apparel strategy.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-superior-group-tightens-fy26-outlook-as-q3-sales-rise-5--314910-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-017", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["[否定]growth", "expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "On Holding laces up for another quarter of growth", "content": "Switzerland's On is expected to post third-quarter revenue of $1.14 billion, up more than 14.5 per cent year on year, as it expands in sportswear.\nIts football entry with Kylian Mbappé, new footwear launches and SURREAL foam technology support its growth plans.\nAnalysts cite EPS of $0.49, a 70 per cent gross margin, 100 planned stores and expansion in Asia-Pacific, Europe and Latin America.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/on-holding-laces-up-for-another-quarter-of-growth-314909-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
